And, where
.it xxxx
is either
.it hasp
or
.it uvac,
.s3
.lp +20 20
/u?/xxxx/pool/stm*	temporary
.lp +20 20
/u?/xxxx/xmit???	queued output
.lp +20 20
/u?/xxxx/xxxxqer	queueing program
.lp +20 20
/u?/xxxx/xxxxlock	null file for lockout
.lp +20 20
/u?/xxxx/xxxxstat	queue status record
.i0
.sh "SEE ALSO"
help(PWB I), sh(PWB I), ascii(V), ebcdic(PWB V), fspec(PWB V), hasp(PWB VI)
.br
PWB RJE \- Guide to IBM Remote Job Entry
.br
PWB RJE \- Guide to UNIVAC Remote Job Entry
.sh DIAGNOSTICS
`non-graphic deleted',
`undefined tab deleted',
`long line detected',
`long line truncated',
`illegal card excised'
\- followed by the resulting card image.
.br
`Errors detected' 
\- type `y' to submit anyway.
.s3
Use help(PWB I) for explanations of error messages.
.sh BUGS
Standard input is read in blocks, and unused bytes are
returned via seek(II).
If standard input is a pipe, multiple arguments
of the form `\-' and `\-:\fIprompt\fR'
should not be used,
nor the logical end-of-file `~.'.
